  "narrative_answer": "Yes, you should be concerned. While STELLA GRILL's inspection scores show significant fluctuation over time—ranging from a catastrophic high of 185 on July 13, 2023 (which resulted in a Summary Permit Suspension due to an imminent health hazard from total lack of cold holding capacity) down to a low score of 10 on February 3, 2026—detailed visual analytics reveal that these score drops represent temporary fixes rather than sustained systemic compliance.\n\nOur detailed multi-chart visual analysis highlights three major facets of Stella Grill's food safety history across 10 inspections between 2022 and 2026:\n\n1. Inspection Score Trajectory & Fluctuation: Stella Grill exhibits a repeating cycle where severe inspection scores (185 in July 2023, 50 in April 2024, 48 in September 2024, and 51 in February 2025) are followed by transient improvements, only for scores to spike back up in subsequent routine visits.\n\n2. Chronic Repeat Critical Violations: The primary risk driver is Stella Grill's status as a repeat critical violator. Rather than isolated incidents, the same high-risk critical code violations recur continuously across multiple years:\n   - Equipment & Food-Contact Surface Cleaning (Code 4.4.82): Cited on 8 out of 10 inspection dates (including dirty ice machines, slicers, and hoods).\n   - Cold Holding Temperature Control (Code 4.3.59): Cited on 5 separate inspection dates with food held above safe temperatures (47°F - 56°F).\n   - Employee Hygiene & Eating/Drinking in Prep Areas (Code 4.2.18): Cited across 4 separate inspection dates.\n   - Chemical Sanitizer Labeling & Concentration (Codes 4.7.2 & 4.4.76): Cited across multiple inspections, including dish machine sanitizer failure.\n   - Unapproved Pesticide / Pest Control Issues (Codes 4.7.13 & 4.7.14): Included unapproved Raid pesticide stored on-site and unshielded rodent bait stations.\n\n3. Critical vs. Non-Critical Severity Distribution: Even when total violation counts drop, critical violations remain present in nearly every inspection cycle (e.g., 10 critical in July 2023, 5 critical in Sept 2024, 4 critical in Feb 2025, and 1 critical in Feb 2026).\n\nAlthough Stella Grill's most recent routine inspection on February 3, 2026 showed a score of 10 (with 1 critical date-marking violation) and the restaurant maintains a high Google rating of 4.5 stars (825 reviews), the historical pattern strongly indicates a recurring risk of compliance regression once formal oversight pressure wanes.",
